diagnosis_text:
The reported fault — PC5 (172.16.10.5) being unable to reach the 172.16.30.x "design group" machines — is not reproducible and leaves no trace in the network state.

**Affected component:** None currently. The complaint targets the inter-VLAN routing path: pc5 (VLAN 10, access via switch1 → mswitch0) through mswitch0 (acting as the Layer 3 distribution switch, advertising 172.16.10.0/24, 172.16.20.0/24, and 172.16.30.0/24 into OSPF area 0) out to switch3 where pc12/pc13/pc14 reside.

**Mechanism:** No fault mechanism is present. OSPF is fully converged across all 9 routers with every router carrying 18 routes and all adjacencies in Full state. mswitch0's VLAN interfaces (vlan10, vlan20, vlan30) are all DR with the correct gateway IPs. infra_sweep confirms all 15 hosts hold valid IPs and default routes. No ACL/nftables rules are installed. No traffic shaping (tbf/netem) is on any interface. No resource pressure or stress tools are running.

**Localization:** Direct pings from pc5 to all three 172.16.30.x hosts (pc12, pc13, pc14) succeed with 0% loss and 1–2 ms RTT, confirming the inter-VLAN forwarding path through mswitch0 is intact end-to-end.

**Root cause:** The reported outage is unconfirmed — no current fault or historical mechanism (no flap process, no carrier-down history, no anomalous log entries) can explain it.

**Fix:** No corrective action required. The network is healthy. If the user experiences the issue again, capture the exact error output and timestamp so a transient event can be investigated.
